RandNonNormal — non-normal random data generator (Pearson distribution system)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Files:   src/rdspd_core/randnonnormal/generator.py
Author:  nadahannad (2023)
Usage:   Vendored into this package as `rdspd_core.randnonnormal`.

Modifications made in this repository (numerically neutral, verified byte-for-byte):
  * module-level imports (they were repeated inside every function);
  * French docstrings added;
  * in the Pearson type IV rejection sampler, `scipy.stats.uniform.rvs()` calls were
    replaced by `numpy.random.random()` — both draw from the same global NumPy random
    stream and produce identical values, but the latter avoids SciPy's per-call overhead.

The generator implements the Pearson distribution system. Users redistributing this
package should satisfy themselves as to the provenance and licensing terms applicable
to this component in their own context.
